[standards/technology/nodejs/STD-TEC-NODE-005-testing.md#22-http-layer-testing-with-supertest]

### 2.2 HTTP Layer Testing with Supertest

**Supertest** is required for HTTP layer (integration) tests. Supertest starts the Express/Fastify application in-process without binding to a port, enabling fast, self-contained HTTP assertions without network overhead.

```typescript
// tests/integration/members.test.ts
import request from 'supertest';
import { app } from '../../src/app';

describe('GET /api/members/:id', () => {
  it('returns 200 with member data for a valid ID', async () => {
    const response = await request(app)
      .get('/api/members/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001')
      .set('Authorization', `Bearer ${validToken}`)
      .set('X-Correlation-ID', 'test-correlation-id')
      .expect(200);

    expect(response.body).toMatchObject({
      id: '00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001',
    });
  });

  it('returns 404 for a non-existent member', async () => {
    const response = await request(app)
      .get('/api/members/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000099')
      .set('Authorization', `Bearer ${validToken}`)
      .expect(404);

    expect(response.body.error.code).toBe('NOT_FOUND');
    expect(response.body.error.correlationId).toBeDefined();
  });
});
```

