[standards/technology/nodejs/STD-TEC-NODE-005-testing.md#51-arrange-act-assert-pattern]

### 5.1 Arrange-Act-Assert Pattern

All tests must follow the Arrange-Act-Assert (AAA) pattern with clear separation:

```typescript
describe('MemberService.getById', () => {
  it('returns the member when found', async () => {
    // Arrange
    const memberId = '00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001';
    const expectedMember: Member = {
      id: memberId,
      planCode: 'PLAN-001',
      status: 'active',
    };
    memberRepository.findById.mockResolvedValue(expectedMember);

    // Act
    const result = await memberService.getById(memberId);

    // Assert
    expect(result).toEqual(expectedMember);
    expect(memberRepository.findById).toHaveBeenCalledWith(memberId);
  });

  it('throws NotFoundError when member does not exist', async () => {
    // Arrange
    memberRepository.findById.mockResolvedValue(null);

    // Act & Assert
    await expect(memberService.getById('nonexistent-id')).rejects.toThrow(NotFoundError);
  });
});
```

page_texts.15:
[standards/technology/nodejs/STD-TEC-NODE-005-testing.md#53-no-any-in-tests]

### 5.3 No `any` in Tests

`any` is prohibited in test code, including mock definitions. Use Jest's `jest.Mocked<T>` or Vitest's `vi.Mocked<T>` utility types to correctly type mocked dependencies:

```typescript
import { MemberRepository } from '../../src/domain/repositories/member.repository';
import { MemberService } from '../../src/domain/services/member.service';

// REQUIRED — typed mock
const memberRepository = {
  findById: jest.fn(),
  save: jest.fn(),
} satisfies jest.MockedObject<MemberRepository>;

const memberService = new MemberService(memberRepository);
```

