[standards/technology/nodejs/STD-TEC-NODE-005-testing.md#61-module-mocking]

### 6.1 Module Mocking

Use `jest.mock()` (Jest) or `vi.mock()` (Vitest) to mock modules at the module boundary. Mock the dependency interface, not its implementation:

```typescript
// Unit test for MemberService — mock the repository module
jest.mock('../../src/infrastructure/db/member.repository');
import { MemberRepository } from '../../src/infrastructure/db/member.repository';

const MockMemberRepository = jest.mocked(MemberRepository);
```

