[standards/technology/nodejs/STD-TEC-NODE-005-testing.md#62-external-http-dependencies]

### 6.2 External HTTP Dependencies

External HTTP calls must be mocked in unit and integration tests. Use `nock` or `jest.fn()` on the HTTP client wrapper. Never make real network calls in automated tests:

```typescript
import nock from 'nock';

beforeEach(() => {
  nock.cleanAll();
});

it('fetches member eligibility from upstream API', async () => {
  nock('https://eligibility-service.internal')
    .get('/eligibility/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001')
    .reply(200, { eligible: true, planCode: 'PLAN-001' });

  const result = await eligibilityClient.check('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001');
  expect(result.eligible).toBe(true);
});
```

