[standards/technology/nodejs/STD-TEC-NODE-005-testing.md#63-database-mocking]

### 6.3 Database Mocking

- Unit tests must mock repository classes; they must not connect to a real database.
- Integration tests may connect to a test database (PostgreSQL in Docker, SQLite in-memory) but must not connect to shared or production databases.
- Use factory functions in `tests/fixtures/` to create consistent test data rather than inline object literals.

```typescript
// tests/fixtures/member.fixtures.ts
import { Member } from '../../src/domain/models/member.model';
import { randomUUID } from 'node:crypto';

export function buildMember(overrides: Partial<Member> = {}): Member {
  return {
    id: randomUUID(),
    planCode: 'PLAN-001',
    status: 'active',
    ...overrides,
  };
}
```

