[standards/technology/nodejs/STD-TEC-NODE-005-testing.md#71-input-validation-tests]

### 7.1 Input Validation Tests

Every Zod or Joi schema must have tests that verify:

- Valid payloads are accepted.
- Payloads with unknown fields are rejected (`.strict()` mode).
- Payloads with missing required fields are rejected with a 400 status.
- Payloads with fields of the wrong type are rejected.
- Boundary cases: empty strings, very long strings, negative numbers.

```typescript
describe('CreateMember validation', () => {
  it('rejects unknown fields in strict mode', async () => {
    const response = await request(app)
      .post('/api/members')
      .send({
        memberId: '00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001',
        dateOfBirth: '1980-01-01',
        planCode: 'PLAN-001',
        injectedField: 'should be rejected',
      })
      .set('Authorization', `Bearer ${validToken}`)
      .expect(400);

    expect(response.body.error.code).toBe('VALIDATION_ERROR');
  });

  it('rejects empty planCode', async () => {
    await request(app)
      .post('/api/members')
      .send({ memberId: '00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001', dateOfBirth: '1980-01-01', planCode: '' })
      .set('Authorization', `Bearer ${validToken}`)
      .expect(400);
  });
});
```

page_texts.22:
[standards/technology/nodejs/STD-TEC-NODE-005-testing.md#72-authentication-bypass-tests]

### 7.2 Authentication Bypass Tests

Protected routes must have tests that verify:

- Requests without an `Authorization` header receive a 401 response.
- Requests with an expired JWT receive a 401 response.
- Requests with a JWT signed with an incorrect key receive a 401 response.
- Requests with a JWT with insufficient claims (wrong role/scope) receive a 403 response.

```typescript
describe('Authentication enforcement', () => {
  it('returns 401 when no Authorization header is present', async () => {
    await request(app)
      .get('/api/members/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001')
      .expect(401);
  });

  it('returns 401 for an expired JWT', async () => {
    await request(app)
      .get('/api/members/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001')
      .set('Authorization', `Bearer ${expiredToken}`)
      .expect(401);
  });

  it('returns 401 for a JWT signed with the wrong key', async () => {
    await request(app)
      .get('/api/members/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001')
      .set('Authorization', `Bearer ${wrongKeyToken}`)
      .expect(401);
  });

  it('returns 403 when the authenticated user lacks the required scope', async () => {
    await request(app)
      .delete('/api/members/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001')
      .set('Authorization', `Bearer ${readOnlyToken}`)
      .expect(403);
  });
});
```

